  {
    "sha": "9d6ebbd62b586f7fe632c9b2feb2dd1c2ea65b86",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDlkNmViYmQ2MmI1ODZmN2ZlNjMyYzliMmZlYjJkZDFjMmVhNjViODY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T18:08:04Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T18:08:04Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): refuse a preset above the machine's last preset row\n\nThe two Heidenhain posts accepted presets 1..6. The Picomax 55 preset\ntable on the 2008 delivery CD has rows 0..5 only, so Q339=+6 names a\nrow that does not exist and the control stops with an alarm.\n\nA machine file can now state controller.work_offset_max, the highest\nwork offset that the control holds. The reader and the raw engine\nrefuse a value that is not a whole number from 1 to 255. The mirror\ncarries the key. The post engine refuses a higher PARAM WorkOffset by\nsetup name before any hook runs, for each post. A machine without the\nkey keeps the post's own limit. fehlmann-picomax55.mch states 5.\n\nFixes #4088\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
